<h2 id="structure">Folder structure</h2>
<p>Everything that matters lives in <code>src/</code>.</p>
<pre><code>portfolio/
├── src/
│   ├── assets/
│   │   └── images/           ← ALL images go here
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── SiteHeader.astro  ← top navigation
│   │   └── CaseStudyNav.astro ← prev/next links
│   ├── data/
│   │   └── projects.ts       ← homepage card data
│   ├── layouts/
│   │   └── Layout.astro      ← HTML wrapper for every page
│   ├── pages/
│   │   ├── index.astro       ← homepage
│   │   ├── about.astro       ← about page
│   │   ├── guide.astro       ← this guide (hidden)
│   │   └── work/
│   │       ├── ui-design.astro
│   │       ├── workshops.astro
│   │       ├── ux-process.astro
│   │       ├── journey-mapping.astro
│   │       ├── design-systems.astro
│   │       ├── research-benchmarking.astro
│   │       └── ai-tooling.astro
│   └── styles/
│       └── case-study.css    ← shared styles for all case study pages
├── public/                   ← static files (favicon etc)
└── astro.config.mjs          ← site config</code></pre>

<h2 id="deploy">How to deploy</h2>
<p>Make your changes, then run this in Terminal:</p>
<pre><code>cd ~/Documents/Code/portfolio && git add -A && git commit -m "describe what you changed" && git push origin main</code></pre>
<p>GitHub Actions builds and deploys automatically. Live in about 2 minutes. Check progress at github.com/asmithdigital/portfolio under the Actions tab.</p>

<div class="warn"><strong>Important:</strong> Two images only exist on your Desktop, not in the repo. Copy them before any deploy:<br><br>
<code>cp ~/Desktop/quick-quote-quinn.png ~/Desktop/detailed-donald.png ~/Documents/Code/portfolio/src/assets/images/</code></div>

<h2 id="images">Adding images</h2>
<h3>Step 1 — Move the image</h3>
<pre><code>mv ~/Desktop/my-image.png ~/Documents/Code/portfolio/src/assets/images/</code></pre>
<p>Use lowercase with hyphens: <code>my-image.png</code> not <code>My Image.png</code></p>

<h3>Step 2 — Import it in the page file</h3>
<p>Open the <code>.astro</code> file. Between the <code>---</code> lines at the top, add:</p>
<pre><code>import myImage from '../../assets/images/my-image.png';</code></pre>

<h3>Step 3 — Use it in HTML</h3>
<pre><code>&lt;Image class="aside-img" src={myImage} alt="Describe the image"
  loading="lazy" decoding="async"
  widths={[480,720]} sizes="(max-width:1200px) 30vw, 480px"/&gt;</code></pre>

<h3>Step 4 — Push</h3>
<pre><code>cd ~/Documents/Code/portfolio && git add -A && git commit -m "Add image" && git push origin main</code></pre>

<h2 id="homepage">Homepage cards</h2>
<p>Cards are defined in <code>src/data/projects.ts</code>. Each card object has these fields:</p>
<pre><code>{
  name: 'UI Design',               // short label on card
  title: 'UI design across...',    // larger heading
  description: 'End-to-end...',    // paragraph text
  background: 'lime',              // lime | cyan | lavender | mint
  href: '/portfolio/work/ui-design', // page the card links to
  image: raaWebsiteImage,          // imported image variable
  alt: 'Describe the image',
}</code></pre>
<div class="tip">Card order in the array = order on the homepage. Move entries up or down to reorder.</div>

<h2 id="case-study">Case study pages</h2>
<p>Every case study page follows the same structure. Copy an existing page and edit it:</p>
<pre><code>---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import CaseStudyNav from '../../components/CaseStudyNav.astro';
import '../../styles/case-study.css';

import myImage from '../../assets/images/my-image.png';
---
&lt;Layout title="Page Title | Andrew Smith" description="..."&gt;
  &lt;a class="skip-link" href="#main-content"&gt;Skip to content&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;div class="case-page"&gt;
    &lt;SiteHeader /&gt;
    &lt;main id="main-content"&gt;

      &lt;section class="case-hero"&gt;
        &lt;p class="eyebrow"&gt;...breadcrumb...&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;h1 class="display-title"&gt;Page heading&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p class="hero-text"&gt;Intro paragraph&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/section&gt;

      &lt;!-- add content sections here --&gt;

      &lt;CaseStudyNav /&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/Layout&gt;</code></pre>

<h2 id="about">About page</h2>
<p>At <code>src/pages/about.astro</code>. Edit text directly. Has its own styles at the bottom of the file — does not use <code>case-study.css</code>.</p>

<h2 id="content-section">Layout: Content section</h2>
<p>Two columns — content left (42rem), image right (fills remaining space). Divider line above.</p>
<div class="pattern-box">
<div class="label">With image on the right</div>
<pre><code>&lt;section class="content-section"&gt;
  &lt;div class="section-content"&gt;
    &lt;p class="section-kicker"&gt;Small caps label&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;Section heading&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Paragraph text.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="section-image"&gt;
    &lt;Image class="aside-img" src={myImage} alt="..."
      loading="lazy" decoding="async"
      widths={[480,720]} sizes="(max-width:1200px) 30vw, 480px"/&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="pattern-box">
<div class="label">Text only — no image</div>
<pre><code>&lt;section class="content-section"&gt;
  &lt;div class="section-content"&gt;
    &lt;p class="section-kicker"&gt;Label&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;Heading&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Text here.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="scroll-gallery">Layout: Scroll gallery</h2>
<p>Horizontal scrolling image gallery. Sits below a content-section or on its own.</p>
<div class="pattern-box">
<div class="label">Standard size — 380x255px (workshops, process pages)</div>
<pre><code>&lt;div class="scroll-section"&gt;
  &lt;p class="scroll-hint-label"&gt;Scroll to see more &lt;span&gt;→&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;div class="image-scroll-track-wrap"&gt;
    &lt;div class="image-scroll-track"&gt;
      &lt;figure class="scroll-fig"&gt;
        &lt;Image class="scroll-img" src={img1} alt="..."
          loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[420,600]} sizes="420px"/&gt;
        &lt;figcaption&gt;Caption&lt;/figcaption&gt;
      &lt;/figure&gt;
      &lt;figure class="scroll-fig"&gt;
        &lt;Image class="scroll-img" src={img2} alt="..."
          loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[420,600]} sizes="420px"/&gt;
        &lt;figcaption&gt;Caption&lt;/figcaption&gt;
      &lt;/figure&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="pattern-box">
<div class="label">Large size — 560x387px (personas, UI screenshots)</div>
<pre><code>&lt;figure class="scroll-fig large"&gt;
  &lt;Image class="scroll-img large" src={img} alt="..."
    loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="600px"/&gt;
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Caption&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="full-image">Layout: Full-width image</h2>
<p>Single large image spanning full content width. Has a border below by default.</p>
<div class="pattern-box">
<pre><code>&lt;section class="full-image-section"&gt;
  &lt;Image class="full-image" src={myImage} alt="..."
    loading="lazy" decoding="async"
    widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
<div class="tip">Add <code>no-border</code> to remove the bottom line: <code>class="full-image-section no-border"</code></div>

<h2 id="lead-image">Layout: Lead image</h2>
<p>Large image at the very top of a page before the first content section. No border below.</p>
<div class="pattern-box">
<pre><code>&lt;section class="lead-image-section"&gt;
  &lt;Image class="lead-image" src={myImage} alt="..."
    decoding="async"
    widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="summary-section">Layout: Summary section</h2>
<p>Wide text block for an opening narrative. Wider than a content-section. Has border below.</p>
<div class="pattern-box">
<pre><code>&lt;section class="summary-section"&gt;
  &lt;p class="section-kicker"&gt;Label&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;Heading&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;div class="summary-body"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;First paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Second paragraph. Can include &lt;a href="/portfolio/work/other-page"&gt;links&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="site-header">Site header</h2>
<p>Top navigation is in <code>src/components/SiteHeader.astro</code>. Edit nav links there. Every page includes it with <code>&lt;SiteHeader /&gt;</code>.</p>

<h2 id="case-nav">Case study nav</h2>
<p>The prev/next links at the bottom of each case study are in <code>src/components/CaseStudyNav.astro</code>. When you add a new page, add it to the pages array there:</p>
<pre><code>const pages = [
  { href: '/portfolio/work/ui-design', label: 'UI Design' },
  { href: '/portfolio/work/workshops', label: 'Workshop Facilitation' },
  { href: '/portfolio/work/my-new-page', label: 'My New Page' }, // add here
];</code></pre>

<h2 id="shared-css">Shared CSS</h2>
<p>All shared layout classes are in <code>src/styles/case-study.css</code>. Every case study page imports it:</p>
<pre><code>import '../../styles/case-study.css';</code></pre>
<p>Page-specific styles go in a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block at the bottom of that page's file only.</p>

<h2 id="new-page">Creating a new page</h2>
<p>1. Copy an existing page as a starting point:</p>
<pre><code>cp ~/Documents/Code/portfolio/src/pages/work/workshops.astro \
   ~/Documents/Code/portfolio/src/pages/work/my-new-page.astro</code></pre>
<p>2. Edit the imports, title, description, and content in the new file</p>
<p>3. Add it to <code>CaseStudyNav.astro</code></p>
<p>4. Add a card for it in <code>src/data/projects.ts</code></p>
<p>5. Push to GitHub</p>
<div class="tip">The URL will be <code>/portfolio/work/my-new-page</code> — matching the filename.</div>

<h2 id="new-card">Adding a homepage card</h2>
<pre><code>// src/data/projects.ts

// 1. Import the banner image at the top of the file
import myBannerImage from '../assets/images/my-banner.png';

// 2. Add to the projects array
{
  name: 'Short name',
  title: 'Longer card heading here.',
  description: 'One or two sentences.',
  background: 'cyan',  // lime | cyan | lavender | mint
  href: '/portfolio/work/my-new-page',
  image: myBannerImage,
  alt: 'Describe the image',
